note: "Three rounds. Round 1 ran five isolated finders with adversarial verification of every candidate: ten candidates, seven refuted, three real, all fixed rather than waived. (1) altitude, important: FlowSource::as_str/parse put the wire tokens on the domain enum. The verifier established the decisive fact - nothing below the API boundary needs the string form, because FlowFilter holds the enum and store.rs compares enum values, so both functions' only non-test callers were in src/api/. W2's own review had refuted the mirror-image proposal (moving the body reason tokens down onto NotCapturedReason) on exactly those grounds, and architecture.html homes wire shape in the API package. Fixed the way W2 established for rfc3339: both directions now live in view.rs as pub(super) source_token/parse_source, one home for the vocabulary, with the round-trip test moved beside the code it tests. (2) efficiency, important: Store::import cloned each flow's request and response inside the ring mutex while insert and set_response both clone before taking it, and the proxy's capture path contends on that same lock, so P2 (critical sections stay minimal) applies to who is stalled rather than who holds. Now cloned before the lock, with the batch still one contiguous critical section so the documented ordering contract is untouched. The measurement corrected the finding's own framing: a verifier's synthetic benchmark reported a ~17x reduction in total hold, but measuring what a real capture actually waits gives ~44ms versus ~49ms on a 2048-flow batch - about 5ms - because a contending capture queues behind the flows still ahead of it rather than the whole batch. This fix ships deliberately WITHOUT a regression test: three were attempted (a lock-held-from-another-thread timing assertion, a concurrent-capture contention test, and a direct hold measurement) and all three passed against the unfixed code, because at any batch size a unit test can afford the two shapes are indistinguishable. Round 2's verifier independently attempted its own design and reached the same conclusion - the only observable difference is when, in wall-clock terms, the clone happens, unreachable through the public Store API without a flaky timing assertion. A test that cannot fail is worse than none because it falsely implies a guard, so the fix is kept on structural grounds and the gap is recorded in the result report. (3) simplification, nit: response_body's fallthrough was two sequential decisions sharing a reason variable, the first with no else; now one match over (marker, size). The verifier proved the single match compiles clippy-clean under this repo's pedantic settings, refuting the concern that it would reintroduce the match_same_arms warning an earlier iteration hit, and confirmed byte-identical semantics across every marker-by-size-by-text combination including a too_large marker with a negative size and a foreign comment at size zero. Round 2 re-verified all three fixes as sound and found one further real finding, against a claim this WU's own test note had made: (4) correctness, important - near_miss_document's docstring and the note both said the generator builds documents whose every member may be wrong-typed, out of range or missing, and it did not. Only the four top-level entry keys were varied, with opaque scalars that fail InRequest/InResponse deserialization outright, so the document died at the outer JSON gate. Measured on the old generator: of 252 cases, 213 stopped at NotJson and only 4 reached entry-level validation, none with a malformed inner member - the deep paths the property named (an out-of-range status, an unnamed header, bad base64 nested in a body, a bad timestamp) were reachable only by the named-example table beside it. Fixed so each member draws from values its own type can hold as well as ones it cannot, with the version weighted toward the supported one because a document rejected at an outer gate never reaches an inner one. Round 3 independently reimplemented the generator against the real unmodified flows_from_har and reproduced the numbers rather than trusting them: at the property's 256-case default, 48-56 entry-level hits and 59-69 full parses per run (versus 4 before), and over 20000 cases all four named deep paths are genuinely and repeatably reached - out-of-range status, unnamed header, bad base64, bad RFC3339. Round 3 also confirmed the property's let _ = assertion is honestly scoped (the WU's claim for it is specifically 'never a panic', epic expected result 7; 'refused with a reason' is separately covered by the example table), that the version weighting is necessary rather than a weakening (without it ~94% of cases die at the version gate), that all six Pools fields are used, and that no comment carrying real rationale was lost. Round 3 found no new findings and verified every numeric claim in the result report. Seven candidates were refuted across the rounds, and in refuting them the finders independently confirmed the WU's load-bearing claims: the parse-before-store invariant is structurally enforced (the handler holds either a complete Vec<Flow> or an error, so 'never a partially-populated store' is a property of the shape rather than a cleanup path), the oldest-first reversal is genuinely exercised rather than tautologically validated, body bytes outrank a declared size, no parsing path can panic, reason_token reads back exactly what not_captured_comment writes, HAR_VERSION and the timestamp format have one definition each, and Store::import shares Ring::evict and announce_evictions with insert. Notable refutations: import returning the accepted count rather than the post-eviction survivor count (UC-6 commits explicitly to 'how many entries it took', DEC-31 accepts eviction as a designed cost, and a survivor count would be stale the moment a concurrent capture lands - differently arbitrary, not more truthful); a SystemTime::from panic path the fuzz generator cannot reach (empirically unreachable, since time 0.3 without large-dates caps years at plus/minus 9999 and the extremes were run without a panic); a params-only postData reading as not-captured (exactly what DEC-30's sentinel-not-invention rule requires, since reconstructing wire bytes from parsed params would fabricate bytes never on the wire); seeded_store duplicating W2's har_fixture_store (extending that helper would churn the insta snapshot it feeds, and the fixtures differ in methods, statuses and body directions); a shared Ring::push extraction (the rubric's explicit 'not its job: inventing new abstractions to force sharing'); decode_body's avoidable copy (the rubric's excluded micro-optimization outside a hot path); the batch's transient ring peak (bounded at ~2x the cap by the route's own body limit, and already the epic's deferred streaming row); Flow public-field mutation after new (a pre-existing in-tree pattern, and host is never stale because the request is complete before construction); and a claim that the plan had specified view.rs for the tokens so the placement was an unrecorded deviation - the plan never mentions the conversion's location at all, so shipping it on the enum resolved an open question rather than deviating. The design dimension did not run: cargo xtask design-scope reports no design artifact and no rendered file in the diff, so this note carries no design section. Gate 0 green at every round."
